🔄 SwiftUI Data Flow Explained (End-to-End) (Day 4)

SwiftUI is completely driven by data flow.

If you understand this, you understand:

how UI updates happen
where bugs come from
how to design scalable apps
🧠 The Core Principle
UI = f(State)

Your UI is a function of state.

🔁 End-to-End Data Flow
User Action
   ↓
View triggers ViewModel
   ↓
ViewModel updates state
   ↓
@Published emits change
   ↓
SwiftUI recomputes body
   ↓
UI updates
1️⃣ Step-by-Step Example
Step 1: User Action
Button("Increment") {
    viewModel.increment()
}
Step 2: ViewModel Updates State
final class CounterViewModel: ObservableObject {
    @Published var count = 0

    func increment() {
        count += 1
    }
}
Step 3: SwiftUI Observes Changes
@StateObject var viewModel = CounterViewModel()

When count changes:

objectWillChange → triggers UI update
Step 4: Body Recomputes
Text("Count: \(viewModel.count)")

SwiftUI recomputes body.

Step 5: Diffing + Rendering

Only the changed part updates:

Text updated → rest unchanged
2️⃣ Data Flow Types

SwiftUI supports multiple flows:

Local State
@State var isOn = false

Flow:

View → View
ViewModel State
@StateObject var vm = VM()

Flow:

View → ViewModel → View
Parent → Child
@Binding var value: Int

Flow:

Parent → Child → Parent
Global State
@EnvironmentObject var session: Session

Flow:

Global → Many Views
3️⃣ Binding — Two-Way Data Flow
TextField("Enter", text: $text)

Binding means:

View ↔ State

Changes in UI update state and vice versa.

4️⃣ One-Way Data Flow (Best Practice)

Preferred architecture:

View → Action → ViewModel → State → View

Why?

predictable
testable
scalable
5️⃣ Common Data Flow Bugs
❌ Bug 1 — State not updating UI
var count = 0 // missing @Published
❌ Bug 2 — ViewModel recreated
@ObservedObject var vm = VM()
❌ Bug 3 — Multiple sources of truth
State duplicated in multiple places
❌ Bug 4 — Wrong binding
TextField(text: .constant(""))

No real data flow.

6️⃣ Single Source of Truth

SwiftUI expects:

One piece of state → one owner

Example:

@StateObject var vm = VM()

Avoid duplicating:

vm.count AND local count
7️⃣ Advanced Flow (Production)
View
 ↓
ViewModel
 ↓
Service Layer
 ↓
Network / DB
