8️⃣ Why SwiftUI Feels Reactive

Because of:

@Published + Combine + Diffing engine

Even without writing Combine manually, SwiftUI uses it internally.

🧠 Interview Power Answer

If asked:

“How does data flow in SwiftUI?”

Answer:

“SwiftUI uses a unidirectional data flow where user actions trigger state changes in a ViewModel, and those changes propagate through property wrappers like @Published, causing the view to recompute and update.”

🔥 Key Insight

SwiftUI is not event-driven like UIKit.
It is state-driven.

⭐ Golden Rules
UI depends on state
State has a single source of truth
Use bindings for two-way flow
Prefer unidirectional flow
Avoid duplicated state
